  → Stage 3: reconstruct definitions and rerun concrete/generated semantics and every positive proof
  • Stage 4: assess claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete satisfying states
  • Stage 5: inventory and audit every K declaration and rule for static soundness
  • Stage 6: create and run a fresh meaningful false proof mutation
  • Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md with verdict
